auxv: report the program, not the loader, as AT_EXECFN

The kernel records the loader's temp file as AT_EXECFN and hands that
record out unchanged through prctl(PR_GET_AUXV) and /proc/self/auxv,
which is where the multi-call coreutils of Ubuntu 25.10 and later look
up which tool they are. Point AT_EXECFN at argv[0] in both, as the
loader already does on the stack: fix up the buffer PR_GET_AUXV fills,
and answer the file with a copy.

Offered upstream as proot-me/proot#446; drop this file once it lands.
